w: |||Low- land las- sie will ye go|Where the hills are clad wi’ snow,|Where be- neath the i- cy steep|
 c3 d c A3 G3 F F4 | G3 A B2 d2 c3 G c4 | G3 A B2 d2 c3 G c4 | F3 B B d3 f3 B (!fermata!g2>f2) | %10
w: Har- dy shep- herds tend their sheep;|Ill nor wae shall thee be- tide,|Row’d with- in my High- land plaid,|Low- land las- sie will ye go _|
 e3 G G2 d2{Bd} c3 G B4 | z16 | z16 || F3 B B2 d2 c3 G B4 | F3 B B2 d2 c G3 B4 | %15
w: Where the hills are clad wi’ snow.|||Then we’ll leave the sheep and goat,|I will launch the bon- nie boat,|
 F3 B B2 d2 c3 G c4 | c3 d c2 A2({FA} G3) F F2 F2 | G3 A B2 d2 c3 G c2 G2 | G3 A B2 d2 c3 G c4 | %19
w: Skim the loch in can- tie glee,|Rest the oars to plea- sure thee, When|chil- ly bree- zes sweep the tide I’ll|row thee in my High- land plaid,|
 F3 B B d3 f3 B (!fermata!g2>f2) | e3 G G2 d2({Bd} c3) G B4 | z16 | z16 | %23
w: Low- land las- sie will ye go _|Where the hills are clad wi’ snow.|||
"^più lento con sentimento" F B3 B2 d2 c3 G B2 F2 | F3 B B2 d2 c3 G B4 | %25
w: High- land lad ye’ve been sae leil, My|haert wad break at our fare- well,|
"^dolce" F3 B B d3 c3 G c4 | c3 d c2"^ad lib" f2({GA} G3) F F4 | %27
w: Lang your love has made me fain,|Tak! oh tak me for your ain|
